sentences.t:
Hinc Augustus agens Italos in proelia Caesar
cum patribus populoque, penatibus et magnis dis,
stans celsa in puppi;

sentences.l:
On this side Augustus, leading the Italians into battle, Caesar,
with the fathers and the people, the Penates and the great gods,
standing on the lofty stern;

sentences.t:
Ipse, sedens niveo candentis limine Phoebi,
dona recognoscit populorum aptatque superbis
postibus;

sentences.l:
He himself, sitting on the snowy of gleaming threshold Phoebus,
the gifts reviews of the peoples and fits them to the proud
doorposts;

sentences.t:
Hic Nomadum genus et discinctos Mulciber Afros,
hic Lelegas Carasque sagittiferosque Gelonos
finxerat;

sentences.l:
Here of the Nomads the race and the ungirt, Mulciber, Africans,
here the Leleges and Carians and the arrow-bearing Geloni
had fashioned;
